{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"staffSize"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLStaffSizeV","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffSize","text":"MXLStaffSize"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"<staff-size>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" element.","type":"text"}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/staffSize"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How large a staff space is on this staff."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffdetails\/staffsize"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails"]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLStaffDetailsV9staffSizeAA0cF0VSgvp","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"staffSize"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLStaffSizeV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLStaffSize"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"role":"symbol","title":"staffSize"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffDetails/staffSize":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/staffSize","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffdetails\/staffsize","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"staffSize","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLStaffSizeV","text":"MXLStaffSize","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How large a staff space is on this staff."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"staffSize"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffSize":{"title":"MXLStaffSize","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStaffSize","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The staff-size element indicates how large a staff space is on this staff, expressed as a percentage of the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"work’s default scaling. Values less than 100 make the staff space smaller while values over 100 make the staff","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"space larger. A staff-type of cue, ossia, or editorial implies a staff-size of less than 100, but the exact"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value is implementation-dependent unless specified here. Staff size affects staff height only, not the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relationship of the staff to the left and right margins."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffSize","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStaffSize"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffsize"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffDetails":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStaffDetails"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLStaffDetails","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLStaffDetails","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffdetails","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The staff-details element is used to indicate different types of staves. The optional number attribute"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specifies the staff number from top to bottom on the system, as with clef. The print-object attribute is used"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"to indicate when a staff is not printed in a part, usually in large scores where empty parts are omitted. It","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"is yes by default. If print-spacing is yes while print-object is no, the score is printed in cutaway format"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"where vertical space is left for the empty part."}]}}}